[[:db/retract 17592186159494 :answer-field/choices 17592186159495] [:db/retract 17592186159494 :answer-field/choices 17592186159496] [:db/retract 17592186159494 :answer-field/choices 17592186159497] [:db/retract 17592186159494 :answer-field/choices 17592186159498] [:db/retract 17592186159494 :answer-field/choices 17592186159499] {:db/id 17592186162107 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-748a2779-e90d-59a2-9916-b0ad2a8182a7" "question-27d2a840-69cf-5325-b960-367fa82827bd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162382 :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3}$ of three nails is drawn from a population. The population has nails of two different lengths, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ and $\\text{10}\\,\\text{cm},$ distributed in the ratio $4:1.$ Calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the nails in the population have lengths $5\\,\\text{cm}$ and $\\text{10}\\,\\text{cm},$ and these are distributed in the ratio $4:1.$ Therefore, to compute the population mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $4+1=5$ nails only with the following lengths:\n\n$$\n5\\,\\text{cm},\\,5\\,\\text{cm},\\,5\\,\\text{cm},\\,5\\,\\text{cm}\\,10\\,\\text{cm}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(4\\cdot 5+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(20+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{5} \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{cm},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(4\\cdot {5}^{2}+{10}^{2})-{6}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(200)-36 \\\\  & =40-36 \\\\  & =4\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the sample size $n=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}=\\frac{4}{3}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}≈1.15\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159494 :answer-field/correct "answer-60c93555-b34b-575f-95b2-f38de1599831" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60c93555-b34b-575f-95b2-f38de1599831" "answer-210567c7-e894-5b02-9ee8-c6893172df38" "answer-ca20eb7d-1ae8-5c45-ab85-1bae5f9c5811" "answer-cfed1752-e352-5a6b-9e2d-7dc6a36ff6ae" "answer-cce28df6-b4e2-5293-9860-139a95e35caa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60c93555-b34b-575f-95b2-f38de1599831" :answer/id #uuid "60c93555-b34b-575f-95b2-f38de1599831" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.15\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-210567c7-e894-5b02-9ee8-c6893172df38" :answer/id #uuid "210567c7-e894-5b02-9ee8-c6893172df38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.18\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca20eb7d-1ae8-5c45-ab85-1bae5f9c5811" :answer/id #uuid "ca20eb7d-1ae8-5c45-ab85-1bae5f9c5811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.32\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfed1752-e352-5a6b-9e2d-7dc6a36ff6ae" :answer/id #uuid "cfed1752-e352-5a6b-9e2d-7dc6a36ff6ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.33\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cce28df6-b4e2-5293-9860-139a95e35caa" :answer/id #uuid "cce28df6-b4e2-5293-9860-139a95e35caa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.24\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-748a2779-e90d-59a2-9916-b0ad2a8182a7" :question/id #uuid "748a2779-e90d-59a2-9916-b0ad2a8182a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-143423" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{20}$ is a sample of size $n=20$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =6$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=1,$ calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance is ${\\sigma }^{2}=1$ and the sample size is $n=20,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{0.05}≈0.22.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5943d631-1c0b-56a0-a90d-e9d31d030f54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5943d631-1c0b-56a0-a90d-e9d31d030f54" :answer-field/id #uuid "5943d631-1c0b-56a0-a90d-e9d31d030f54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25a99cc8-8701-579f-b7ef-cb9e7b7f1e7c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-785ab3f2-459a-5180-8933-34aa9440618c" "answer-0a2ebf1d-6b21-517e-8473-6b5520ced24c" "answer-25a99cc8-8701-579f-b7ef-cb9e7b7f1e7c" "answer-55e8daa5-4432-5f7f-b7b9-25ac21b5f238" "answer-92d71196-a3a0-5ab1-b5f5-5721df71e75d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-785ab3f2-459a-5180-8933-34aa9440618c" :answer/id #uuid "785ab3f2-459a-5180-8933-34aa9440618c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a2ebf1d-6b21-517e-8473-6b5520ced24c" :answer/id #uuid "0a2ebf1d-6b21-517e-8473-6b5520ced24c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25a99cc8-8701-579f-b7ef-cb9e7b7f1e7c" :answer/id #uuid "25a99cc8-8701-579f-b7ef-cb9e7b7f1e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55e8daa5-4432-5f7f-b7b9-25ac21b5f238" :answer/id #uuid "55e8daa5-4432-5f7f-b7b9-25ac21b5f238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92d71196-a3a0-5ab1-b5f5-5721df71e75d" :answer/id #uuid "92d71196-a3a0-5ab1-b5f5-5721df71e75d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.71" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-27d2a840-69cf-5325-b960-367fa82827bd" :question/id #uuid "27d2a840-69cf-5325-b960-367fa82827bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-143424" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{8}$ is a sample of size $n=8$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =30$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=16,$ calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance is ${\\sigma }^{2}=16$ and the sample size is $n=8,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{2}≈1.41.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5fa84345-5063-5b45-a9a8-f4e3ac36fb05"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5fa84345-5063-5b45-a9a8-f4e3ac36fb05" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fa84345-5063-5b45-a9a8-f4e3ac36fb05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-19e33d38-75d1-531e-92cf-f39947aea28c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84db3eb9-187b-5476-8ae3-4fc97bb737af" "answer-b7436ec0-730a-5723-89b9-c51e09d25df2" "answer-19e33d38-75d1-531e-92cf-f39947aea28c" "answer-3e89daf0-19fa-53f4-b72d-31d6ed1621bb" "answer-116200b8-f0e0-5d54-986b-cdb0d1f93684"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84db3eb9-187b-5476-8ae3-4fc97bb737af" :answer/id #uuid "84db3eb9-187b-5476-8ae3-4fc97bb737af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7436ec0-730a-5723-89b9-c51e09d25df2" :answer/id #uuid "b7436ec0-730a-5723-89b9-c51e09d25df2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19e33d38-75d1-531e-92cf-f39947aea28c" :answer/id #uuid "19e33d38-75d1-531e-92cf-f39947aea28c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e89daf0-19fa-53f4-b72d-31d6ed1621bb" :answer/id #uuid "3e89daf0-19fa-53f4-b72d-31d6ed1621bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.77" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-116200b8-f0e0-5d54-986b-cdb0d1f93684" :answer/id #uuid "116200b8-f0e0-5d54-986b-cdb0d1f93684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162108 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d1b6912a-93b9-571b-8ea5-2d8ab50d8a7a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d1b6912a-93b9-571b-8ea5-2d8ab50d8a7a" :question/id #uuid "d1b6912a-93b9-571b-8ea5-2d8ab50d8a7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143486" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ of $n$ bushes is drawn from a population. The population has bushes of two different heights, $4\\,\\text{ft}$ and $5\\,\\text{ft},$ distributed in the ratio $3:2.$ Determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $0.01\\,\\text{ft}.$" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the bushes in the population have heights $4\\,\\text{ft}$ and $5\\,\\text{ft},$ and these are distributed in the ratio $3:2.$ Therefore, to compute the population's mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $3+2=5$ bushes only with the following heights:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\text{ft},\\,4\\,\\text{ft},\\,4\\,\\text{ft},\\,5\\,\\text{ft},\\,5\\,\\text{ft}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(12+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{22}{5} \\\\  & =4.4\\,\\text{ft},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot {4}^{2}+2\\cdot {5}^{2})-{4.4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(98)-19.36 \\\\  & =19.6-19.36 \\\\  & =0.24\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{0.24},$ and we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\frac{0.24}{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.01\\,\\text{ft}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{0.24}{n}} & <0.01 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{\\sqrt{0.24}}{0.01} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{\\frac{0.24}{{0.01}^{2}}} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{2\\,400} \\\\ n & >2\\,400.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=2\\,401.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e022f4b-ff74-5796-8a0f-0137d56c7a63"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e022f4b-ff74-5796-8a0f-0137d56c7a63" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e022f4b-ff74-5796-8a0f-0137d56c7a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ae7b1ee7-ec01-58b0-9c87-f819883b152a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8e2a8088-2557-53ce-b8f2-d4dcab799771" "answer-0e7b64bf-b6ca-57e9-aaa1-181aed3d622b" "answer-160f3d12-5eab-5995-9f63-e81fe88512ce" "answer-ae7b1ee7-ec01-58b0-9c87-f819883b152a" "answer-78a69e66-0db0-56b0-9e49-ac78e00b8276"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2a8088-2557-53ce-b8f2-d4dcab799771" :answer/id #uuid "8e2a8088-2557-53ce-b8f2-d4dcab799771" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "194" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e7b64bf-b6ca-57e9-aaa1-181aed3d622b" :answer/id #uuid "0e7b64bf-b6ca-57e9-aaa1-181aed3d622b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "197" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-160f3d12-5eab-5995-9f63-e81fe88512ce" :answer/id #uuid "160f3d12-5eab-5995-9f63-e81fe88512ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "241" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae7b1ee7-ec01-58b0-9c87-f819883b152a" :answer/id #uuid "ae7b1ee7-ec01-58b0-9c87-f819883b152a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,401" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78a69e66-0db0-56b0-9e49-ac78e00b8276" :answer/id #uuid "78a69e66-0db0-56b0-9e49-ac78e00b8276" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "441" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162394 :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ of $n$ employees is drawn from a population. The population has employees with two different working hours, $38\\,\\text{h/week}$ and $40\\,\\text{h/week},$ distributed in the ratio $3:1.$ Determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than  $0.5\\,\\text{h/week}.$" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the employees in the population have working hours $38\\,\\text{h/week}$ and $40\\,\\text{h/week},$ and these are distributed in the ratio $3:1.$ Therefore, to compute the population's mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $3+1=4$ employees only with the following working hours:\n\n$$\n38\\,\\text{h/week},\\,38\\,\\text{h/week},\\,38\\,\\text{h/week},\\,40\\,\\text{h/week}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(3\\cdot 38+40) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(114+40) \\\\  & =\\frac{154}{4} \\\\  & =38.5\\,\\text{h/week},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(3\\cdot {38}^{2}+{40}^{2})-{38.5}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(5\\,932)-1\\,482.25 \\\\  & =1\\,483-1\\,482.25 \\\\  & =0.75\\,{(\\text{h/week})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{0.75},$ and we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\frac{0.75}{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.5\\,\\text{h/week}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{0.75}{n}} & <0.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{\\sqrt{0.75}}{0.5} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{\\frac{0.75}{{0.5}^{2}}} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{\\frac{0.75}{0.25}} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\sqrt{3} \\\\ n & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159566 :answer-field/correct 17592186159571 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7fa56d66-b299-55c7-8a43-47f002ff063b" :activity/id #uuid "7fa56d66-b299-55c7-8a43-47f002ff063b" :activity/title "Variance of Sample Means" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049674 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-26fcd0c3-24b3-5951-9b42-4462bd2fac3d" "step-c77ffddd-aed2-56b6-b329-53374af11408" "step-3e79243e-67ec-56e0-9d13-5331e6398a52" "step-fe9fb3ff-fe13-546b-ad08-eeb0688c4db2" "step-a723e053-b0fa-5616-b5a2-e66027d73c57"] :activity/first-step "step-26fcd0c3-24b3-5951-9b42-4462bd2fac3d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-26fcd0c3-24b3-5951-9b42-4462bd2fac3d" :step/id #uuid "26fcd0c3-24b3-5951-9b42-4462bd2fac3d" :step/content 17592186162382 :step/next "step-c77ffddd-aed2-56b6-b329-53374af11408" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c77ffddd-aed2-56b6-b329-53374af11408" :step/id #uuid "c77ffddd-aed2-56b6-b329-53374af11408" :step/content "question-748a2779-e90d-59a2-9916-b0ad2a8182a7" :step/next "step-3e79243e-67ec-56e0-9d13-5331e6398a52" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3e79243e-67ec-56e0-9d13-5331e6398a52" :step/id #uuid "3e79243e-67ec-56e0-9d13-5331e6398a52" :step/content "question-27d2a840-69cf-5325-b960-367fa82827bd" :step/next "step-fe9fb3ff-fe13-546b-ad08-eeb0688c4db2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fe9fb3ff-fe13-546b-ad08-eeb0688c4db2" :step/id #uuid "fe9fb3ff-fe13-546b-ad08-eeb0688c4db2" :step/content "question-d1b6912a-93b9-571b-8ea5-2d8ab50d8a7a" :step/next "step-a723e053-b0fa-5616-b5a2-e66027d73c57" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a723e053-b0fa-5616-b5a2-e66027d73c57" :step/id #uuid "a723e053-b0fa-5616-b5a2-e66027d73c57" :step/content 17592186162394 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
